    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on navigating a collection of middling matchups where high-ceiling speed assets are noticeably absent from the active lineup. **Travis Bazzana** emerges as our strongest play with a 56.66 score, benefiting from an advantageous pairing against Montero, K. The projection reflects a significant boost from his favorable platoon split (+7%) and a weak SP_xERA of 4.43, making him our primary source of offensive efficiency today. **Josh Naylor** follows closely at 54.98; while he faces a tough southpaw in Fried, his consistent recent performance keeps his floor stable, even though the dynamic platoon disadvantage drags his efficiency below the 60-point threshold for a \"Strong\" start.\n\nThe remainder of the lineup reflects the scarcity of our elite options. **Seiya Suzuki** (52.65) holds the OF1 spot, leaning on his high-leverage position in the two-hole (+8% order boost) to offset the talent of Cavalli on the mound. **Jose Caballero** remains our most volatile start; his 44.61 score is propped up by the necessity of his role in the infield, though he faces a stiff challenge against a high-caliber arm in Gilbert, L. With stalwarts like **Corbin Carroll** and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined by team off-days and **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** continuing their frustrating stints on the IL, we are effectively playing a \"bridge\" lineup. **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** are all currently evaluated as secondary to these starters or unavailable due to the schedule, forcing us to remain patient while managing our daily cap efficiency.",
